    contentElement.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', '          <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n            <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n              <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/2184886-how-does-symbolic-math-toolbox-define-differentiation-of-a-complex-function/?s_tid=ans_lp_feed_leaf\">How Does Symbolic Math Toolbox Define Differentiation of a Complex Function?<\/a><\/p>\n              <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                  <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                    <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                      <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/35216\'>\n                        <img alt=\"Paul\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"/responsive_image/75/75/0/0/0/profile/35216\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, \'/responsive_image/100/0/0/0/0/cache/matlabcentral/profiles/profilepic_default.gif\');\"><\/img><\/a>\n                      <\/div>\n                      <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/35216\'>Paul<\/a> \n                        on 11 Sep 2026                        \n                      <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> The doc page diff - Differentiate symbolic expression or function - MATLAB is essentially silent on how diff handles differentiation of complex functions. All it says in the Tips section is: \"For complex arguments of abs and sign, the diff functi...<\/p>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\">\n                    <strong>Tags<\/strong>: \n                    <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22complex+differentiation%22\">complex differentiation<\/a>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\">\n                    <ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\">\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"vote\"><\/span> 1<\/li>\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span> 229<\/li>  \n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-comment feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span> 5<\/li>                          \n                    <\/ul>\n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\">\n                  <div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\">\n                    <div class=\"answers_meta\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"2 Answers\">\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_count\">2<\/span>\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answers<\/span>\n                    <\/div>           \n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n              <\/div>\n            <\/div>\n          <\/div>\n          <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n            <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n              <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/2184872-best-practice-for-passing-structure-to-a-function-and-adding-new-fields-when-returning-it/?s_tid=ans_lp_feed_leaf\">Best practice for passing structure to a function and adding new fields when returning it<\/a><\/p>\n              <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                  <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                    <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                      <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/28668323\'>\n                        <img alt=\"Oshani\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"/responsive_image/75/75/0/0/0/profile/28668323\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, \'/responsive_image/100/0/0/0/0/cache/matlabcentral/profiles/profilepic_default.gif\');\"><\/img><\/a>\n                      <\/div>\n                      <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/28668323\'>Oshani<\/a> \n                        on 9 Sep 2026                        \n                      <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> This is more a style question than anything else. I\'m passing a structure to a function, adding some fields to the structure, and returning the structure. Which of the following is considered best practice? Option 1: defining the fields you want ...<\/p>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\">\n                    <strong>Tags<\/strong>: \n                    <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22struct%22\">struct<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22structures%22\">structures<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22variables%22\">variables<\/a>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\">\n                    <ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\">\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span> 0<\/li>\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span> 161<\/li>  \n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-comment feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span> 8<\/li>                          \n                    <\/ul>\n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\">\n                  <div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\">\n                    <div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer, 1 Answer\">\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_count\">2<\/span>\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answers<\/span>\n                    <\/div>           \n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n              <\/div>\n            <\/div>\n          <\/div>\n          <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n            <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n              <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/2184821-how-to-find-start-and-end-points-of-signal-in-data-file/?s_tid=ans_lp_feed_leaf\">How to find start and end points of signal in data file?<\/a><\/p>\n              <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                  <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                    <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                      <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/10373363\'>\n                        <img alt=\"Daniel Flisek\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"/responsive_image/75/75/0/0/0/profile/10373363\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, \'/responsive_image/100/0/0/0/0/cache/matlabcentral/profiles/profilepic_default.gif\');\"><\/img><\/a>\n                      <\/div>\n                      <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/10373363\'>Daniel Flisek<\/a> \n                        on 3 Sep 2026                        \n                      <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> I have several hundred data files containing electric field over time measurements from a real system. The data has ~20 seconds of lead and trail time where the signal is off, so the data at the beginning and end of the file is just noise. I want...<\/p>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\">\n                    <strong>Tags<\/strong>: \n                    <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22data+file%22\">data file<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22filtering%22\">filtering<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22signal%22\">signal<\/a>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\">\n                    <ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\">\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span> 0<\/li>\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span> 126<\/li>  \n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-comment feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span> 2<\/li>                          \n                    <\/ul>\n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\">\n                  <div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\">\n                    <div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer, 1 Answer\">\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_count\">2<\/span>\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answers<\/span>\n                    <\/div>           \n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n              <\/div>\n            <\/div>\n          <\/div>\n          <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n            <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n              <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/2184744-realtime-model-runs-slower-after-change-to-2026a/?s_tid=ans_lp_feed_leaf\">Realtime model runs slower after change to 2026a<\/a><\/p>\n              <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                  <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                    <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                      <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/12796386\'>\n                        <img alt=\"John Christensen\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"/responsive_image/75/75/0/0/0/profile/12796386\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, \'/responsive_image/100/0/0/0/0/cache/matlabcentral/profiles/profilepic_default.gif\');\"><\/img><\/a>\n                      <\/div>\n                      <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/12796386\'>John Christensen<\/a> \n                        on 26 Aug 2026                        \n                      <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> I have a simulink model running realtime that I was running using simulink 2023b on a speedgoat performance machine. I saw that 2026a had switched to a new RTOS so I updated my speedgoat to dual-boot and then compiled my model in 2026a. The model...<\/p>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\">\n                    <strong>Tags<\/strong>: \n                    <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22simulink%22\">simulink<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22realtime%22\">realtime<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22real-time%22\">real-time<\/a>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\">\n                    <ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\">\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span> 0<\/li>\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span> 123<\/li>  \n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-comment feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span> 4<\/li>                          \n                    <\/ul>\n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\">\n                  <div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\">\n                    <div class=\"answers_meta\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"0 Answers\">\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_count\">0<\/span>\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answers<\/span>\n                    <\/div>           \n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n              <\/div>\n            <\/div>\n          <\/div>\n          <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n            <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n              <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/2184892-installed-antenna-on-uav-fails-to-model/?s_tid=ans_lp_feed_leaf\">Installed antenna on UAV fails to model<\/a><\/p>\n              <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                  <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                    <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                      <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/21324121\'>\n                        <img alt=\"Richard\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"/responsive_image/75/75/0/0/0/profile/21324121\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, \'/responsive_image/100/0/0/0/0/cache/matlabcentral/profiles/profilepic_default.gif\');\"><\/img><\/a>\n                      <\/div>\n                      <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/21324121\'>Richard<\/a> \n                        on 11 Sep 2026                        \n                      <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> I am trying to model the installed performance of an antenna on a UAV (about 4m wingspan). I created a simple \"dummy\" UAV in Blender to try things out. I exported this as an STL file which passes stlFileChecker with no errors. To keep things simp...<\/p>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\">\n                    <strong>Tags<\/strong>: \n                    <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22mesh%22\">mesh<\/a>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\">\n                    <ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\">\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span> 0<\/li>\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span> 85<\/li>  \n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-comment feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span> 2<\/li>                          \n                    <\/ul>\n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\">\n                  <div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\">\n                    <div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer\">\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_count\">1<\/span>\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answer<\/span>\n                    <\/div>           \n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n              <\/div>\n            <\/div>\n          <\/div>\n              <div class=\"panel panel-default panel_sidebar -left lp-share-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n  <div class=\"panel-body w-100 add_border_color_orange\">\n    <p class=\"category_label share_section add_font_color_orange\"><strong>SHARE YOUR KNOWLEDGE<\/strong><\/p>\n    <p class=\"add_margin_12\"><span id=\"share_help\">Help<\/span> <a class=\"author_inline analyticsMlcProfileModal\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\"/matlabcentral/profile/authors/11764002\">CoderMinga<\/a>\n\n<\/p>\n    <p class=\"h3 share_question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/2184402-when-generating-an-fmu-from-a-simulink-model-the-parameters-are-not-correctly-reflected-in-the-resu\">When generating an FMU from a Simulink model, the parameters are not correctly reflected in the resulting FMU.<\/a><\/p>\n    <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n      <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n        <p class=\"share_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\">\nI built a simple boost converter model and wanted to generate an FMU. I set the relevant parameters (such as Ts, C, L, and R) as variables and initialized them using an inifcn function. The FMU was generated successfully, but when I load the FMU, only Vin appears as a parameter; all the other p...<\/p>\n        <div class=\"d-flex flex-row align-items-center gap-3 flex-wrap\">\n          <div class=\"search_result_meta add_margin_0 feed_stats flex-grow-1\">\n            <ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\">\n              <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span> 0<\/li>\n              <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span> 30<\/li>\n              <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-comment feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span> 0<\/li>                         \n            <\/ul>\n          <\/div>\n          <div class=\"d-flex flex-row flex-nowrap align-items-center ms-auto gap-3\">\n            <p class=\"search_result_meta add_margin_0\"><a id=\"answer_all\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/answer/?s_tid=ans_lp_unanswered\">View all unanswered questions<\/a><\/p>\n            <p class=\"search_result_meta add_margin_0\"><a id=\"answer_this\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/2184402-when-generating-an-fmu-from-a-simulink-model-the-parameters-are-not-correctly-reflected-in-the-resu/?s_tid=ans_lp_share\" class=\"btn btn_color_blue btn-block add_padding_10\">Answer this question<\/a><\/p>\n          <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n      <\/div>\n    <\/div>\n  <\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n          <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n            <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n              <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/2184876-different-coloured-regions-on-a-scatter-plot/?s_tid=ans_lp_feed_leaf\">Different coloured regions on a scatter plot<\/a><\/p>\n              <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                  <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                    <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                      <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/40730256\'>\n                        <img alt=\"Felicity\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"/responsive_image/75/75/0/0/0/profile/40730256\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, \'/responsive_image/100/0/0/0/0/cache/matlabcentral/profiles/profilepic_default.gif\');\"><\/img><\/a>\n                      <\/div>\n                      <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/40730256\'>Felicity<\/a> \n                        on 10 Sep 2026                        \n                      <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> I have a g-g diagram where I want to display different regions in different colours (so right acceleration is one colour, pure acceleration is a different one, left acceleration is different, pure left cornering is different and so on). I was abl...<\/p>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta answer-tag-list tags_ans_lp\">\n                    <strong>Tags<\/strong>: \n                    <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22scatter%22\">scatter<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22plot%22\">plot<\/a><span class=\"separator\"><\/span> <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/?term=tag%3A%22color%22\">color<\/a>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <div class=\"search_result_meta feed_stats\">\n                    <ul class=\"list-inline -has_list_separators\">\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-like feed_votes\" aria-label=\"votes\"><\/span> 0<\/li>\n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-watch feed_views\" aria-label=\"views\"><\/span> 81<\/li>  \n                      <li class=\"list-inline-item\"><span class=\"icon-comment feed_comments\" aria-label=\"comments\"><\/span> 0<\/li>                          \n                    <\/ul>\n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"lp-answers-card_sidebar\">\n                  <div class=\"search_result_supplemental_content justify-content-center align-items-center d-flex flex-column\">\n                    <div class=\"answers_meta -is_accepted\" data-accepted-label=\"Accepted Answer\" data-bs-toggle=\"tooltip\" data-bs-title=\"1 Accepted Answer, 1 Answer\">\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_count\">2<\/span>\n                      <span class=\"answers_meta_label\">answers<\/span>\n                    <\/div>           \n                  <\/div>\n                <\/div>\n              <\/div>\n            <\/div>\n          <\/div>\n          <div class=\"panel panel-default lp-answers-card search_result add_padding_0\">\n            <div class=\"panel-body w-100\">\n              <p class=\"h3 question_title add_margin_12\"><a class=\"card-title\" href=\"/matlabcentral/answers/2184840-inconsistent-observation-input-type-of-getactionimpl-method-in-custom-reinforcement-learning-agent-c/?s_tid=ans_lp_feed_leaf\">Inconsistent observation input type of getActionImpl method in Custom Reinforcement Learning Agent Class<\/a><\/p>\n              <div class=\"d-flex flex-row\">\n                <div class=\"search_result_content\">\n                  <div class=\"post_meta search_result_meta\">\n                    <div class=\"d-flex align-items-center\">\n                      <div class=\"flex-shrink-0\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/15310007\'>\n                        <img alt=\"Chuguang Pan\" class=\"rounded-circle community_profile_image\" src=\"/responsive_image/75/75/0/0/0/profile/15310007\" width=\"24\" onerror=\"img_not_found(this, \'/responsive_image/100/0/0/0/0/cache/matlabcentral/profiles/profilepic_default.gif\');\"><\/img><\/a>\n                      <\/div>\n                      <div class=\"flex-grow-1 ms-2\">\n                        <a class=\"author_inline\" data-locale-id=\"en\" href=\'/matlabcentral/profile/authors/15310007\'>Chuguang Pan<\/a> \n                        on 5 Sep 2026                        \n                      <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n                  <\/div>\n                  <p class=\"post_body text-wrap d-none d-md-block search_result_desc\"> I want to construct custom Reinforcement Learning (RL) agent based on template class provided by MATLAB Example. After constructing the custom RL